cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "LSV Analysis: iR Compensation and Tafel Slope Analysis"
abstract: >-
  A Streamlit application with two independent workflows for electrochemical
  polarization data: automated ohmic-drop (iR) compensation of linear-sweep
  voltammetry (LSV) data using the uncompensated resistance (Ru) estimated
  from an EIS Nyquist-arc circle fit, and Tafel slope analysis (with RHE
  reference-electrode conversion and HER/OER/ORR mechanistic interpretation).
type: software
version: 1.1.0
